00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:09,408
The Guardian reports that British households still face heavy pressure from energy bills, even after the government promised relief.

2
00:00:09,358 --> 00:00:16,755
Experts say the UK electricity system remains expensive because gas often sets the market price.

3
00:00:16,755 --> 00:00:25,755
The debate shows how Europe's cost-of-living problem is linked to energy policy, climate plans and the speed of grid reform.

